Description: Native multi-touch for the Cowboy Machine browser
 Gives Xvnc an XI2 direct-touch device beside its pointer and accepts
 multi-touch contacts from RFB clients that negotiate them.
 .
 - Parameter AcceptTouchEvents (default off, not overridable through the VNC
   extension). Off, the server behaves exactly like the stock build: no
   touch device, no acknowledgement, and message 193 is an unknown message.
 - On, the core pointer is typed XI_MOUSE and a slave "TigerVNC touch"
   (XI_TOUCHSCREEN, XIDirectTouch, 10 contacts) is attached to it, so X
   clients see an ordinary touchscreen laptop for every viewer.
 - A client requests pseudo-encoding -1883 in SetEncodings; the server
   answers once with message 192 (u8 type, u8 version = 1, u8 contacts = 10).
   Only then may the client send message 193 (KasmVNC layout: u8 type,
   u8 state 0 begin / 1 update / 2 end, u32 id, u16 x, u16 y, big endian,
   framebuffer pixels). Any other state is a protocol error.
 - Contacts are slots of one pool shared by every screen of the process,
   since all of them feed the one XI2 device (at most 10 in total); a
   duplicate begin, an update or end of an unknown id and a begin beyond the
   bound are ignored; coordinates are clamped to the framebuffer.
 - Every contact a connection leaves active ends when the connection
   closes. Without pointer permission (access rights or AcceptPointerEvents)
   nothing new is accepted, but active contacts still end: at once when
   AcceptPointerEvents is turned off through the VNC extension, otherwise on
   the client's next touch message, at their last accepted positions.
